Bitburner Simplified Chinese Userscript — licensing overview

This repository contains material under different licenses.

1. Independently written userscript implementation and tooling
   Files under src/, scripts/ and tests/ (except copied upstream fixtures and
   excerpts) are licensed under the MIT License in licenses/MIT.txt.

2. Bitburner material and derivative translations
   English excerpts, reference fixtures, map labels, translated game text and
   translations/candidates.json derive from Bitburner by Daniel Y Xie and
   contributors, including the Chinese contributions in PR #3068 by FRzhuizhu.
   They retain Apache License 2.0 WITH the Commons Clause License Condition
   v1.0, reproduced in full in licenses/Bitburner.txt. No right to remove the
   Commons Clause is granted by this repository's MIT-licensed code.

3. The standalone bitburner-zh-cn.user.js bundles both categories.
   Redistribution must preserve both notices and the upstream license,
   including the Commons Clause. The combined distribution is source-available;
   it must not be described as an unrestricted MIT, plain Apache-2.0, or
   OSI-approved open-source distribution.

See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for pinned provenance and modification details.
Third-party development dependencies retain their own package licenses and are
not bundled into the userscript. This project is unofficial and is not endorsed
by the Bitburner maintainers or the author of the reference translation.
